      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub> Make feedback idempotency atomic** When two retries with the same scoped `traceId` and `clientKey` arrive concurrently, both can complete this lookup before either creates its row, so both feedback records are persisted and later analytics count the supposedly idempotent submission twice. Use an atomic upsert or a unique scoped key covering the trace, client key, tenant, and user instead of a separate read followed by create. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎."
