      "body": "This maps every error caught after the signal becomes aborted to the abort reason, even when the error was already classified from an HTTP response. If `response.body.cancel()` completes after the timer fires, a known 401/403/provider failure becomes retryable `PROVIDER_TIMEOUT`; preserve the HTTP error and substitute the signal reason only for an actual abort rejection. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Preserve classified Google response errors ## Affected sites - `langfn/typescript/src/models/google.ts:312` — response-body cancellation is awaited before the HTTP status is classified. - `langfn/typescript/src/models/google.ts:329` — an abort that occurs during that wait unconditionally overrides the subsequently thrown provider error. - `langfn/typescript/tests/google-native.test.ts:189-232` — covers aborts during headers and successful-response consumption, but not delayed cleanup of a non-OK response. ## Required outcome - Keep typed timeout/caller-abort identity when fetch or body consumption rejects because of cancellation. - Do not replace an already classified provider/auth/rate-limit error merely because the signal became aborted during cleanup. ## Suggested approach - Gate abort-reason substitution on the caught error being an abort rejection, and add a non-OK response whose body cancellation resolves after the timeout. ```` </details>"
