      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub> Bound LangFn HTTP request bodies** When this router is exposed without an upstream body limit, any client able to reach `/complete`, `/chat`, `/stream`, `/embed`, or `/feedback` can send an arbitrarily large body, and `parseJsonBody()` buffers it through `request.json()` before validation. The shared router already supports streaming enforcement through `maxBodyBytes`, but this factory neither sets it nor exposes it as an option, so a large request can exhaust the server process before authentication-aware application logic rejects the payload. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎."
